1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,220
Listen to a talk in an anthropology class.

2
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:07,403
Man:

3
00:00:07,403 --> 00:00:17,150
In the first half of the 20th century, an anthropological movement emerged, called the Culture and Personality School.

4
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:24,703
According to the Culture and Personality school, people's personalities are a result of the

5
00:00:24,703 --> 00:00:25,765
culture they live in,

6
00:00:25,765 --> 00:00:34,040
and not just based on biology, like not just inherited from their biological parents.

7
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:40,557
For example, how children in a culture experience food, the foods they eat, how

8
00:00:40,557 --> 00:00:45,250
it's prepared, this shapes their individual tastes and preferences.

9
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:51,290
One of the anthropologists most associated with this movement was Ruth Benedict.

10
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:58,140
Benedict studied and embraced the principles of cultural relativism.

11
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:05,226
So according to cultural relativism, all cultures should be studied on their own terms

12
00:01:05,226 --> 00:01:09,160
and not judged against some external measure.

13
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:17,264
So cultures in, say, Egypt, belong to Egypt and shouldn't be the standard of

14
00:01:17,264 --> 00:01:19,270
what all cultures should try to be.

15
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:24,888
Ruth Benedict refuted the dominant anthropology theory at the time,

16
00:01:24,888 --> 00:01:32,090
which stated that there was a hierarchy of cultures, some advanced, others not.

17
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:34,250
Rejecting that took courage.

18
00:01:34,250 --> 00:01:37,240
And I think the field is better for it.

19
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:44,150
Benedict was also influenced by psychology, especially Gestalt ideas.

20
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:53,030
According to Gestalt psychology, a personality is an integrated whole, not just a list of traits.

21
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:57,945
Like, If you see a painting of a landscape, you're looking at a whole landscape

22
00:01:57,945 --> 00:02:03,160
and not just say, a hill, trees and a farmhouse.

23
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:10,901
Benedict said that cultures were the same way, a whole coherent system with patterns of values

24
00:02:10,901 --> 00:02:12,064
and behaviors,

25
00:02:12,064 --> 00:02:18,140
and more than just a set of characteristics.
